Z||000013||fiero56||06-23-2001||11:49 PM||||Stay away from RAM clutches if at all possible. Although mine has been reliable for daily driver(25K miles so far)it...sucks.<P>Everytime I drive the car when cold, the clutch causes terrible dash/dental work chatter until it has <B>thoroughly</B> warmed up(15 minutes in stop 'n' go). It is impossible to smoothly drive the car until the clutch set is warmed. When warm, the clutch is barely able to hold my very tired 2.8 to the tranny. The clutch is physically unable to bite hard enough to break the tires loose when I try. <P>Pedal feel is light, and when warm engauges very smoothly, but I will never use another one. As I recall Ed Parks uses stock LUK clutches even on the 3.4 with no problems.||||reg||1
Z||000014||tgowens||06-24-2001||01:07 AM||||Bruce, first of all, (why am I mentioning this again......it is my understanding that Archie did not get the same clutch the Fiero Shop sells for the V-6 - secondly, it is not <I>my</I> parts department - as I have said over and over, I am here restoring <I>my</I> 5 cars - I am using the Kevlar clutch (as are some others on this forum) and have had no problem whatsoever with them. Robert asked the question and I answered it - I don't even recall that I said <I>where</I> it came from!<P>Are you a Fiero Shop customer? I'm just curious. I'm not meaning anything by that but just wondered what you had bought from them.||||reg||1
Z||000015||RobertVol||06-24-2001||02:05 AM||||Thanks Terry ...I may contact you off list for more info. <P>BTW guys.....look at my first post.... what does it say about the whole Fieroshop thing? <P>Let it go. I don't listen to all that ranting on. If "I" want a Fieroshop clutch I would get one. A fool and his money may soon be departed but it is "MY" money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>It may only be just me, but that whole thing concerning  that clutch post fiasco smelled a little funny. When it gets personal there is alot more than meets they eye, and no one and I mean no one "Really" knows what happened and I will make my own judgement.<P>But again ....Thanks for the input Bruce and Terry.  <P><BR>2birds - Hey buddy ! could you send me the info you have on them? thanks ! <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RobsGT2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||2birds||06-29-2001||01:14 AM||||Sorry it took me so long to get back to you, Robert.  (Sea) Duty called.<P>Dealer's Equipment is in downtown Jacksonville, just off Riverside drive.  I drive by landmarks in Jax, so coming from the north, I get off of I-95 the exit just before the new bridge, then head left toward downtown, until I get to Riverside.  I turn left then, and Dealer's Equipment is right by the Olsen Tire, about 1/2 mile, on the left.  <BR>My pressure plate is a standard 4 spring LUK.  I've had the RAM 6 sping LUK disc, OEM replacement (about 40,000 miles), and a dealer installed clutch (4 spring LUK disc, about 60,000, same as the original clutch).  I've put about 6,000 miles on this one since last summer; so far, so good.  I figure $120 beats the arm and a leg some places want, since mine is stock.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Formula88||11-16-2001||05:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>Stay away from RAM clutches if at all possible. Although mine has been reliable for daily driver(25K miles so far)it...sucks.<P>Everytime I drive the car when cold, the clutch causes terrible dash/dental work chatter until it has [b]thoroughly</B> warmed up(15 minutes in stop 'n' go). It is impossible to smoothly drive the car until the clutch set is warmed. When warm, the clutch is barely able to hold my very tired 2.8 to the tranny. The clutch is physically unable to bite hard enough to break the tires loose when I try. <P>Pedal feel is light, and when warm engauges very smoothly, but I will never use another one. As I recall Ed Parks uses stock LUK clutches even on the 3.4 with no problems.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Picking this back up....which RAM clutch are you using, the HD or the Racing Kevlar clutch?  I've got the regular HD RAM and have noticed none of the problems you mention in 20K miles of daily driving.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||avengador1||11-16-2001||06:34 PM||||Same here. I have the HD Ram clutch and have not experienced any problems even when dumping the clutch occasionally.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
